INSERT INTO public.document_chunks (id, document_id, chunk_text, chunk_index, embedding) VALUES (
  '18490021-02c2-40a8-be31-d95ccc60153d',
  '2621c631-cdab-4871-a143-dbf9a3daf97a',
  '30-60-90 Day Onboarding Plan & Questions Introduction: Welcome to [Company Name]! We are excited to have you on board. Your success is important to us, and this onboarding plan is designed to help you transition smoothly into your new role. First 30 Days: Orientation and Learning: Days 1-5: Orientation and Company Overview Complete new employee paperwork and orientation sessions. Attend company-wide meetings and introductions to key team members. Review company policies and procedures. Days 6-15: Departmental Deep Dive Meet with team members individually. Shadow key roles within the department. Attend departmental meetings to understand workflows. Days 16-30: Training and Skill Development Participate in relevant training sessions. Set up meetings with key stakeholders. Begin working on small tasks and projects to apply knowledge. Next 30 Days: Integration and Project Involvement: Days 31-45: Project Involvement Begin contributing to team projects. Take on additional responsibilities gradually. Seek feedback on performance. Days 46-60: Skill Enhancement Identify areas for skill improvement and work on them. Attend workshops or training sessions to enhance skills. Establish regular check-ins with supervisor for feedback. Final 30 Days: Independence and Goal Setting: Days 61-75: Independent Contribution Work more independently on assigned tasks and projects. Demonstrate proficiency in key responsibilities. Seek opportunities to take the lead on certain projects. Days 76-90: Goal Setting and Future Planning Meet with supervisor to discuss performance and set future goals. Identify areas for continued growth and development. Participate in performance reviews and goal-setting discussions. 30-60-90 Day Onboarding Questions: First 30 Days: What are your initial impressions of the company culture and work environment? Have you had sufficient training and orientation to understand your role and responsibilities? What are your short-term goals for the first 30 days, and how do you plan to achieve them? Are there any challenges or obstacles you''ve encountered during your first month, and how can we support you in overcoming them? Have you had the opportunity to meet and collaborate with your team members and other colleagues? What feedback or suggestions do you have for improving the onboarding process based on your experience so far? Next 30 Days (Days 31-60): How have your responsibilities evolved since starting with the company? What new skills or knowledge have you acquired during your first two months? Are there any areas where you feel you need additional training or support to excel in your role? Have you established clear goals and priorities for the next',
  0,
