  'paragraph, rebuild the answer with 3 parts 1) DEFINITION — What is it? 2) PROCESS — How does it work? 3) EFFECT / USE — What does it do or where is it used? Example: “Erosion is a morphological operation. It uses a structuring element and shrinks objects. It is used for noise removal and object separation.” 11. MORNING 15–20 MINUTE REVISION Do NOT reread everything 1. Say the pipeline aloud: IMAGE → SMOOTH → MORPHOLOGY → FLOOD → RESIZE → CONVOLUTION → THRESHOLD. 2. Recall filters: MEAN / GAUSSIAN / MEDIAN / BILATERAL / BOX. 3. Recall morphology: EROSION = SHRINK; DILATION = GROW; OPENING = E→D; CLOSING = D→E. 4. Recall flood fill: SEED; 4-connected; 8-connected; tolerance. 5. Recall interpolation: 1 → 4 → 16 → 64 + AREA. 6. Recall convolution: SLIDE → MULTIPLY → ADD; padding = preserve size; high-pass = sharpen. 7. Recall threshold: GLOBAL = one; ADAPTIVE = local; output = binary. 8. Recall OpenCV commands: imread, resize, adaptiveThreshold, __version__, opencv-python, BGR. 9. For any long answer: DEFINITION → PROCESS → EFFECT/USE. 12. FINAL ONE-LINE MEMORY MAP OpenCV reads → Image is pixels/matrix → Smooth noise → Morphology changes shape → Flood Fill fills region → Resize changes size → Convolution filters → Threshold separates. UNIT 1 — QUICK REVISION COMPLETE',
  4,
